{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>You have turned</b> — Happy is the one who lives until his soul's fulfillment, to serve his Creator and to know His deeds, for this he was created." "And the meaning of <b>you loosened my sackcloth</b> — by way of likening, as one mourning over himself." "And the meaning of <b>you girded me</b> — for strengthening."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:59.385993130Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}